## Event Data Mocking in InngestTestEngine

The incoming event data can be mocked and is always specified as an array of events to allow also mocking batches. 

All mocks can be specified either when creating an InngestTestEngine instance or for each individual execution:

```javascript
// Set the events for every execution
const t = new InngestTestEngine({
  function: helloWorld,
  // mocks here
});

// Or for just one execution
t.execute({
  // mocks here
});
```

## Custom Event Transformation

You can provide a transformCtx function when instantiating InngestTestEngine to add custom mocks including event data:

```javascript
const t = new InngestTestEngine({
  function: helloWorld,
  transformCtx: (ctx) => {
    return {
      ...ctx,
      event: someCustomThing,
    };
  },
});
```

While the search results don't show a specific phoneNumber example, the pattern for passing event data with custom fields would follow the structure shown above. You would mock the event data array with your phoneNumber field as part of the event object when setting up your test.

The @inngest/test package was last published 2 months ago (version 0.1.7), making it a relatively recent testing tool for Inngest functions in 2024-2025.

